+# Fetching notes
+
+## Rate limit
+
+No visits-per-window, window length, or post-breach cooldown value for this
+fetch is recorded anywhere in this repo (checked `GATE1.md`, `manifest.tsv`,
+`unavailable.tsv`, the `research/` notes, and `muninn-bench` source). `GATE1.md`
+says only that "fetching is rate-limited" and that it is why just 115 of 323
+manifest entries were on disk at measurement time — no numbers behind that
+statement survive. Not writing a figure here rather than inventing one.
+
+## Host
+
+`manifest.tsv`'s header records a single source: files were located via GitHub
+code search (grep.app) on 2026-09-12 and fetched raw from
+`raw.githubusercontent.com`. No CDN or mirror host (e.g. jsDelivr, statically.io)
+appears anywhere in the repo for this corpus — everything went through that one
+host.
